# AICC Multi-IDE Engineering Standard — Code Owners
#
# Portability note: this file uses GitHub TEAM handles (ORG/team form resolves
# at runtime to whatever organization the repository lives in). Replace the
# placeholder team slugs below with your organization's real teams when the
# standard is adopted. No personal usernames or account identifiers are
# hardcoded, so this ports cleanly to Huron's corporate GitHub.

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
*                                   @ORG/aicc-engineering-maintainers

# Shared, tool-independent governance, policy, and evidence contract.
/docs/engineering-standard/         @ORG/aicc-engineering-maintainers @ORG/aicc-governance
/engineering-hub/evidence/          @ORG/aicc-engineering-maintainers @ORG/aicc-governance

# GitHub enforcement surface (CI, CODEOWNERS, PR templates, workflows).
/.github/                           @ORG/aicc-engineering-maintainers @ORG/aicc-platform

# Branch-protection and version policy require governance sign-off.
/docs/engineering-standard/02-framework-version-policy.md   @ORG/aicc-governance
/docs/engineering-standard/framework-version.json           @ORG/aicc-governance
/docs/engineering-standard/04-branch-protection.md          @ORG/aicc-platform

# Tool-specific onboarding adapters are owned by the maintainers; each stays
# separate so no shared rule depends on a single tool.
/docs/engineering-standard/onboarding/adapters/             @ORG/aicc-engineering-maintainers
